IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `era-types`
IMPORT `era-periods`
IMPORT `era-notice`
IMPORT `era-unfair-dismissal`
IMPORT `era-redundancy`
IMPORT `era-goal`

-- Employment Rights Act 1996 (UK) — the encoder's tests.
-- Expected values are worked by hand from the Act, not from the code.

§ `Tests`

GIVEN dob IS A DATE, start IS A DATE, pay IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Employee`
`born` dob `, started` start `, paid` pay MEANS `Employee` OF dob, start, pay

-- Started 1 January 2020.
from2020 MEANS `born` (Date 1 1 1990) `, started` (Date 1 1 2020) `, paid` 500

GIVEN how IS A `How the contract ended`, notice IS A MAYBE DATE, ended IS A DATE, during IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Termination`
`ended by` how `, notice` notice `, ended` ended `, during the employer's notice` during MEANS
    `Termination` OF how, notice, ended, during

GIVEN notice IS A MAYBE DATE, ended IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Termination`
`the employer ended it, notice` notice `, on` ended MEANS
    `ended by` `terminated by the employer` `, notice` notice `, ended` ended `, during the employer's notice` FALSE

-- Fields: s 64(2), no qualifying period, presented, conciliation, late
-- allowed, found unfair, reason, reductions, redundancy payments.
GIVEN presented IS A MAYBE DATE, conc IS A MAYBE `Early conciliation`
GIVETH AN `Unfair dismissal facts`
`a complaint presented` presented `, conciliation` conc MEANS
    `Unfair dismissal facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, presented, conc, FALSE, TRUE, `an ordinary reason`, 0, 0

GIVEN reason IS A `Reason for dismissal`, reductions IS A NUMBER, paid IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Unfair dismissal facts`
`found unfair for` reason `, reduced by` reductions `, redundancy paid` paid MEANS
    `Unfair dismissal facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, JUST (Date 1 1 2025), NOTHING, FALSE, TRUE, reason, reductions, paid

GIVEN s64 IS A BOOLEAN, none IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Unfair dismissal facts`
`qualifying facts, s 64(2)` s64 `, no period` none MEANS
    `Unfair dismissal facts` OF s64, none, NOTHING, NOTHING, FALSE, TRUE, `an ordinary reason`, 0, 0

noUD MEANS `qualifying facts, s 64(2)` FALSE `, no period` FALSE

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Early conciliation`
`ACAS from` a `to` b MEANS JUST (`Early conciliation` OF a, b)

-- Fields: redundancy, s 140, s 141, other, paid, written claim, reference,
-- s 111 complaint, conciliation, just and equitable.
GIVEN red IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, s140 IS A BOOLEAN, written IS A MAYBE DATE, referred IS A MAYBE DATE,
      conc IS A MAYBE `Early conciliation`, justEq IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Redundancy facts`
`redundancy` red `, s 140` s140 `, claimed` written `, referred` referred `, conciliation` conc `, just` justEq MEANS
    `Redundancy facts` OF red, s140, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, written, referred, NOTHING, conc, justEq

GIVEN written IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Redundancy facts`
`redundant, claimed on` written MEANS
    `redundancy` (JUST TRUE) `, s 140` FALSE `, claimed` written `, referred` NOTHING `, conciliation` NOTHING `, just` FALSE

§§ `Goal 1 — minimum notice (s 86)`

-- Less than one month: none. One month from 1 January 2020 ends 31 January.
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employer must give` from2020 `on` (Date 30 1 2020) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employee must give` from2020 `on` (Date 30 1 2020) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employer must give` from2020 `on` (Date 31 1 2020) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employee must give` from2020 `on` (Date 31 1 2020) EQUALS 1
-- Two years end 31 December 2021.
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employer must give` from2020 `on` (Date 30 12 2021) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employer must give` from2020 `on` (Date 31 12 2021) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employer must give` from2020 `on` (Date 30 12 2024) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employer must give` from2020 `on` (Date 31 12 2024) EQUALS 5
-- The employee's notice stays one week.
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employee must give` from2020 `on` (Date 31 12 2024) EQUALS 1
-- Twelve years and over: twelve weeks.
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employer must give` (`born` (Date 1 1 1970) `, started` (Date 1 1 2000) `, paid` 500) `on` (Date 1 6 2025) EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employer must give` (`born` (Date 1 1 1970) `, started` (Date 1 1 2013) `, paid` 500) `on` (Date 30 12 2024) EQUALS 11
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employer must give` (`born` (Date 1 1 1970) `, started` (Date 1 1 2013) `, paid` 500) `on` (Date 31 12 2024) EQUALS 12
-- From 31 January 2026 the month ends on 28 February (no 31 February).
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employer must give` (`born` (Date 1 1 1990) `, started` (Date 31 1 2026) `, paid` 500) `on` (Date 27 2 2026) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employer must give` (`born` (Date 1 1 1990) `, started` (Date 31 1 2026) `, paid` 500) `on` (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS 1
-- From 29 February 2024 two years end on 28 February 2026.
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employer must give` (`born` (Date 1 1 1990) `, started` (Date 29 2 2024) `, paid` 500) `on` (Date 27 2 2026) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the notice in weeks the employer must give` (`born` (Date 1 1 1990) `, started` (Date 29 2 2024) `, paid` 500) `on` (Date 28 2 2026) EQUALS 2
-- Five weeks' notice given on Tuesday 31 December 2024 expires on 4 February 2025.
#ASSERT `the day the employer's statutory notice given on` (Date 31 12 2024) `to` from2020 `would expire` EQUALS Date 4 2 2025
#ASSERT `the day the employer's statutory notice given on` (Date 15 1 2020) `to` from2020 `would expire` EQUALS Date 15 1 2020

§§ `The later effective date of termination (ss 97(2), (4)) and relevant date (s 145(5))`

-- Summary dismissal on 20 December 2021: one week's notice would have expired
-- on 27 December, still short of two years (31 December).
summary20 MEANS `the employer ended it, notice` NOTHING `, on` (Date 20 12 2021)
#ASSERT `the effective date of termination for ss 108(1) and 119(1) of` from2020 `and` summary20 EQUALS Date 27 12 2021
#ASSERT NOT (`the qualifying period in s 108 is met by` from2020 `for` summary20 `with` noUD)
-- Summary dismissal on 26 December 2021: the notice would have run to
-- 2 January 2022, so the two years are reached.
summary26 MEANS `the employer ended it, notice` NOTHING `, on` (Date 26 12 2021)
#ASSERT `the effective date of termination for ss 108(1) and 119(1) of` from2020 `and` summary26 EQUALS Date 2 1 2022
#ASSERT `the effective date of termination under s 97(1) of` summary26 EQUALS Date 26 12 2021
#ASSERT `the qualifying period in s 108 is met by` from2020 `for` summary26 `with` noUD
#ASSERT `the relevant date for ss 155 and 162(1) of` from2020 `and` summary26 EQUALS Date 2 1 2022
-- Four weeks' notice given 1 December 2021, expiring 29 December: the
-- statutory week would have expired on 8 December, earlier, so no change.
notice1Dec MEANS `the employer ended it, notice` (JUST (Date 1 12 2021)) `, on` (Date 29 12 2021)
#ASSERT `the effective date of termination for ss 108(1) and 119(1) of` from2020 `and` notice1Dec EQUALS Date 29 12 2021
#ASSERT NOT (`the qualifying period in s 108 is met by` from2020 `for` notice1Dec `with` noUD)
-- Constructive dismissal on 26 December 2021 (s 97(4)): extended to 2 January
-- 2022 for unfair dismissal, but s 145(5) has no employee limb.
constructive26 MEANS `ended by` `terminated by the employee, entitled to do so without notice by the employer's conduct` `, notice` NOTHING `, ended` (Date 26 12 2021) `, during the employer's notice` FALSE
#ASSERT `the effective date of termination for ss 108(1) and 119(1) of` from2020 `and` constructive26 EQUALS Date 2 1 2022
#ASSERT `the qualifying period in s 108 is met by` from2020 `for` constructive26 `with` noUD
#ASSERT `the relevant date for ss 155 and 162(1) of` from2020 `and` constructive26 EQUALS Date 26 12 2021
#ASSERT NOT (`the qualifying period in s 155 is met by` from2020 `for` constructive26)
-- s 97(4)(b): during the employer's notice, no extension.
constructiveDuring MEANS `ended by` `terminated by the employee, entitled to do so without notice by the employer's conduct` `, notice` NOTHING `, ended` (Date 26 12 2021) `, during the employer's notice` TRUE
#ASSERT `the effective date of termination for ss 108(1) and 119(1) of` from2020 `and` constructiveDuring EQUALS Date 26 12 2021
-- A limited-term contract ending: neither extension.
limited26 MEANS `ended by` `a limited-term contract ended by the limiting event without renewal` `, notice` NOTHING `, ended` (Date 26 12 2021) `, during the employer's notice` FALSE
#ASSERT `the effective date of termination for ss 108(1) and 119(1) of` from2020 `and` limited26 EQUALS Date 26 12 2021

§§ `Goal 2 — unfair dismissal`

-- s 95(1): resignation is not dismissal.
#ASSERT NOT (`the employee is dismissed under s 95(1) by` (`ended by` `terminated by the employee otherwise` `, notice` NOTHING `, ended` (Date 26 12 2021) `, during the employer's notice` FALSE))
#ASSERT `the employee is dismissed under s 95(1) by` constructive26
#ASSERT `the employee is dismissed under s 95(1) by` limited26
-- s 108(2): one month for a s 64(2) dismissal; s 108(3)-(5): no period.
#ASSERT `the qualifying period in s 108 is met by` from2020 `for` (`the employer ended it, notice` NOTHING `, on` (Date 1 3 2020)) `with` (`qualifying facts, s 64(2)` TRUE `, no period` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the qualifying period in s 108 is met by` from2020 `for` (`the employer ended it, notice` NOTHING `, on` (Date 20 1 2020)) `with` (`qualifying facts, s 64(2)` TRUE `, no period` FALSE))
#ASSERT `the qualifying period in s 108 is met by` from2020 `for` (`the employer ended it, notice` NOTHING `, on` (Date 20 1 2020)) `with` (`qualifying facts, s 64(2)` FALSE `, no period` TRUE)

-- s 111(2)(a): three months beginning with the effective date of termination.
GIVEN ended IS A DATE, conc IS A MAYBE `Early conciliation`
GIVETH A DATE
`the UD limit, ended` ended `, conciliation` conc MEANS
    `the last day to present an unfair dismissal complaint for` (`the employer ended it, notice` NOTHING `, on` ended) `with` (`a complaint presented` NOTHING `, conciliation` conc)

#ASSERT `the UD limit, ended` (Date 15 6 2026) `, conciliation` NOTHING EQUALS Date 14 9 2026
#ASSERT `the UD limit, ended` (Date 1 3 2026) `, conciliation` NOTHING EQUALS Date 31 5 2026
#ASSERT `the UD limit, ended` (Date 31 8 2026) `, conciliation` NOTHING EQUALS Date 30 11 2026
#ASSERT `the UD limit, ended` (Date 30 11 2026) `, conciliation` NOTHING EQUALS Date 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the UD limit, ended` (Date 28 2 2027) `, conciliation` NOTHING EQUALS Date 27 5 2027
-- s 207B(3): 1-15 August stops 14 days: 28 September; (4) does not bite.
#ASSERT `the UD limit, ended` (Date 15 6 2026) `, conciliation` (`ACAS from` (Date 1 8 2026) `to` (Date 15 8 2026)) EQUALS Date 28 9 2026
-- s 207B(4): 1-10 September gives 23 September, inside the window that ends
-- one month after Day B, so 10 October.
#ASSERT `the UD limit, ended` (Date 15 6 2026) `, conciliation` (`ACAS from` (Date 1 9 2026) `to` (Date 10 9 2026)) EQUALS Date 10 10 2026
-- Day A after the limit: no extension.
#ASSERT `the UD limit, ended` (Date 15 6 2026) `, conciliation` (`ACAS from` (Date 20 9 2026) `to` (Date 25 9 2026)) EQUALS Date 14 9 2026

-- s 111(2)-(3): when the tribunal may consider the complaint.
june15 MEANS `the employer ended it, notice` (JUST (Date 1 6 2026)) `, on` (Date 15 6 2026)
#ASSERT `the tribunal may consider the unfair dismissal complaint for` june15 `with` (`a complaint presented` (JUST (Date 14 9 2026)) `, conciliation` NOTHING)
#ASSERT NOT (`the tribunal may consider the unfair dismissal complaint for` june15 `with` (`a complaint presented` (JUST (Date 15 9 2026)) `, conciliation` NOTHING))
-- s 111(3): after notice given, before the effective date of termination.
#ASSERT `the tribunal may consider the unfair dismissal complaint for` june15 `with` (`a complaint presented` (JUST (Date 10 6 2026)) `, conciliation` NOTHING)

§§ `The basic award (ss 119-122, 227)`

-- Born 1 January 1980, continuously employed from 1 January 2010, notice
-- given 1 October 2024 (twelve weeks would end 24 December), contract ended
-- 31 December 2024. Fifteen years: 2021-2024 at 41 or over (4 × 1.5 = 6),
-- 2010-2020 (11 × 1) = 17 weeks. A week's pay of £800 is capped at £751:
-- £12,767.
older MEANS `born` (Date 1 1 1980) `, started` (Date 1 1 2010) `, paid` 800
oct1 MEANS `the employer ended it, notice` (JUST (Date 1 10 2024)) `, on` (Date 31 12 2024)
#ASSERT `the weeks' pay for the years of employment of` older `ending with` (Date 31 12 2024) EQUALS 17
#ASSERT `the basic award for` older `and` oct1 `with` (`found unfair for` `an ordinary reason` `, reduced by` 0 `, redundancy paid` 0) EQUALS 12767
-- s 122: reductions, and a redundancy payment for the same dismissal.
#ASSERT `the basic award for` older `and` oct1 `with` (`found unfair for` `an ordinary reason` `, reduced by` 1000 `, redundancy paid` 2000) EQUALS 9767
#ASSERT `the basic award for` older `and` oct1 `with` (`found unfair for` `an ordinary reason` `, reduced by` 5000 `, redundancy paid` 12767) EQUALS 0
-- s 121: two weeks' pay, capped: £1,502.
#ASSERT `the basic award for` older `and` oct1 `with` (`found unfair for` `redundancy, within s 121` `, reduced by` 0 `, redundancy paid` 0) EQUALS 1502

-- Born 1 June 2000, from 1 June 2019 to 31 May 2025 (notice of five weeks
-- given 1 April 2025 would end 6 May). Six years: first days 1 June 2024 and
-- 2023 and 2022 (22 on 1 June 2022) at one week; 2021, 2020, 2019 at half:
-- 4.5 weeks × £400 = £1,800.
young MEANS `born` (Date 1 6 2000) `, started` (Date 1 6 2019) `, paid` 400
may31 MEANS `the employer ended it, notice` (JUST (Date 1 4 2025)) `, on` (Date 31 5 2025)
#ASSERT `the basic award for` young `and` may31 `with` (`found unfair for` `an ordinary reason` `, reduced by` 0 `, redundancy paid` 0) EQUALS 1800
-- Born 2 June 2000: 22 only on 2 June 2022, after that year began: 4 weeks.
#ASSERT `the basic award for` (`born` (Date 2 6 2000) `, started` (Date 1 6 2019) `, paid` 400) `and` may31 `with` (`found unfair for` `an ordinary reason` `, reduced by` 0 `, redundancy paid` 0) EQUALS 1600

-- Born 1 January 1950, from 1 January 1990 to 31 December 2024: 35 years,
-- only the last twenty count, all at one and a half: 30 × £751 = £22,530.
veteran MEANS `born` (Date 1 1 1950) `, started` (Date 1 1 1990) `, paid` 900
#ASSERT `the basic award for` veteran `and` oct1 `with` (`found unfair for` `an ordinary reason` `, reduced by` 0 `, redundancy paid` 0) EQUALS 22530

-- s 120(1), (1C): minimum amounts. Two years at one week, £500: £1,000.
twoYears MEANS `the employer ended it, notice` (JUST (Date 1 12 2021)) `, on` (Date 31 12 2021)
#ASSERT `the basic award for` from2020 `and` twoYears `with` (`found unfair for` `an ordinary reason` `, reduced by` 0 `, redundancy paid` 0) EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the basic award for` from2020 `and` twoYears `with` (`found unfair for` `a reason listed in s 120(1)` `, reduced by` 0 `, redundancy paid` 0) EQUALS 9157
#ASSERT `the basic award for` from2020 `and` twoYears `with` (`found unfair for` `a blacklist reason under s 104F` `, reduced by` 0 `, redundancy paid` 0) EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `the basic award for` from2020 `and` twoYears `with` (`found unfair for` `a reason listed in s 120(1)` `, reduced by` 157 `, redundancy paid` 0) EQUALS 9000

§§ `Goal 3 — redundancy payment`

-- Same facts as the basic award: £12,767.
#ASSERT `the amount of a redundancy payment under s 162 for` older `and` oct1 EQUALS 12767
#ASSERT `the amount of a redundancy payment under s 162 for` young `and` may31 EQUALS 1800
-- s 145(5): summary dismissal on 26 December 2021 counts to 2 January 2022:
-- two years at one week (born 1990), £1,000.
#ASSERT `the amount of a redundancy payment under s 162 for` from2020 `and` summary26 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `is entitled to a redundancy payment` from2020 `for` summary26 `with` (`redundant, claimed on` (JUST (Date 1 2 2022)))

-- s 164(1): six months beginning with 31 December 2024 end on 30 June 2025.
#ASSERT `the last day of the s 164(1) period for` oct1 EQUALS Date 30 6 2025
#ASSERT `is entitled to a redundancy payment` older `for` oct1 `with` (`redundant, claimed on` (JUST (Date 30 6 2025)))
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled to a redundancy payment` older `for` oct1 `with` (`redundant, claimed on` (JUST (Date 1 7 2025))))
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled to a redundancy payment` older `for` oct1 `with` (`redundant, claimed on` NOTHING))
-- s 164(2): within the next six months (to 31 December 2025) and just and
-- equitable.
#ASSERT `is entitled to a redundancy payment` older `for` oct1 `with` (`redundancy` (JUST TRUE) `, s 140` FALSE `, claimed` (JUST (Date 1 7 2025)) `, referred` NOTHING `, conciliation` NOTHING `, just` TRUE)
#ASSERT `is entitled to a redundancy payment` older `for` oct1 `with` (`redundancy` (JUST TRUE) `, s 140` FALSE `, claimed` (JUST (Date 31 12 2025)) `, referred` NOTHING `, conciliation` NOTHING `, just` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled to a redundancy payment` older `for` oct1 `with` (`redundancy` (JUST TRUE) `, s 140` FALSE `, claimed` (JUST (Date 1 1 2026)) `, referred` NOTHING `, conciliation` NOTHING `, just` TRUE))

-- s 164(5) with s 207B: relevant date 15 March 2025, limit 14 September; ACAS
-- 1-20 September gives 3 October, inside the window to 20 October, so 20
-- October for a tribunal reference — but not for a written claim.
march15 MEANS `the employer ended it, notice` (JUST (Date 1 1 2025)) `, on` (Date 15 3 2025)
#ASSERT `the last day of the s 164(1) period for` march15 EQUALS Date 14 9 2025
#ASSERT `is entitled to a redundancy payment` older `for` march15 `with` (`redundancy` (JUST TRUE) `, s 140` FALSE `, claimed` NOTHING `, referred` (JUST (Date 20 10 2025)) `, conciliation` (`ACAS from` (Date 1 9 2025) `to` (Date 20 9 2025)) `, just` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled to a redundancy payment` older `for` march15 `with` (`redundancy` (JUST TRUE) `, s 140` FALSE `, claimed` NOTHING `, referred` (JUST (Date 21 10 2025)) `, conciliation` (`ACAS from` (Date 1 9 2025) `to` (Date 20 9 2025)) `, just` FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled to a redundancy payment` older `for` march15 `with` (`redundancy` (JUST TRUE) `, s 140` FALSE `, claimed` (JUST (Date 15 10 2025)) `, referred` NOTHING `, conciliation` (`ACAS from` (Date 1 9 2025) `to` (Date 20 9 2025)) `, just` FALSE))

-- s 163(2): not proved either way, presumed; the contrary proved, no right.
#ASSERT `is entitled to a redundancy payment` older `for` oct1 `with` (`redundancy` NOTHING `, s 140` FALSE `, claimed` (JUST (Date 1 2 2025)) `, referred` NOTHING `, conciliation` NOTHING `, just` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled to a redundancy payment` older `for` oct1 `with` (`redundancy` (JUST FALSE) `, s 140` FALSE `, claimed` (JUST (Date 1 2 2025)) `, referred` NOTHING `, conciliation` NOTHING `, just` FALSE))
-- s 140(1): summary dismissal for conduct.
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled to a redundancy payment` older `for` oct1 `with` (`redundancy` (JUST TRUE) `, s 140` TRUE `, claimed` (JUST (Date 1 2 2025)) `, referred` NOTHING `, conciliation` NOTHING `, just` FALSE))
-- s 155: constructive dismissal short of two years (no s 145(5)); and
-- resignation is not dismissal.
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled to a redundancy payment` from2020 `for` constructive26 `with` (`redundant, claimed on` (JUST (Date 1 2 2022))))
#ASSERT NOT (`is entitled to a redundancy payment` older `for` (`ended by` `terminated by the employee otherwise` `, notice` NOTHING `, ended` (Date 31 12 2024) `, during the employer's notice` FALSE) `with` (`redundant, claimed on` (JUST (Date 1 2 2025))))

§§ `The top-level goal`

-- Older employee, made redundant on notice ending 31 December 2024, claims
-- the redundancy payment on 1 February 2025 and complains of unfair
-- dismissal on 1 January 2025; found unfair, the redundancy payment set off.
udFound MEANS `found unfair for` `an ordinary reason` `, reduced by` 0 `, redundancy paid` 12767
claimedFeb MEANS `redundant, claimed on` (JUST (Date 1 2 2025))
theCase MEANS `Dismissal case` OF older, oct1, udFound, claimedFeb
pos MEANS `the dismissal position for` theCase
#ASSERT pos's `weeks of notice the employer had to give` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT pos's `weeks of notice the employee had to give` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT pos's `effective date of termination` EQUALS Date 31 12 2024
#ASSERT pos's `effective date of termination for ss 108 and 119` EQUALS Date 31 12 2024
#ASSERT pos's `is dismissed`
#ASSERT pos's `meets the unfair dismissal qualifying period`
#ASSERT pos's `last day to present an unfair dismissal complaint` EQUALS Date 30 3 2025
#ASSERT pos's `basic award` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT pos's `entitled to a redundancy payment`
#ASSERT pos's `redundancy payment` EQUALS 12767
#ASSERT pos's `last day of the s 164(1) period` EQUALS Date 30 6 2025

-- Not found unfair: no basic award; short service: no redundancy payment.
shortCase MEANS `Dismissal case` OF from2020, notice1Dec, noUD, (`redundant, claimed on` (JUST (Date 1 2 2022)))
shortPos MEANS `the dismissal position for` shortCase
#ASSERT shortPos's `weeks of notice the employer had to give` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT NOT (shortPos's `meets the unfair dismissal qualifying period`)
#ASSERT shortPos's `basic award` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT NOT (shortPos's `entitled to a redundancy payment`)
#ASSERT shortPos's `redundancy payment` EQUALS 0
